/*!

*\page put Put (Digital Out)
*
* Send data to a digital pin or a digital bus. The internal definition of these GPIO is DigitalInOut and configured as output.<BR>
* Before using a bus you need to create it using create_reg instruction.
*<span style='color:blue'><em><H4> Syntax: </H4></em></span>
*<B> put GPIO_NAME/BUS_name, VARIABLE_NAME/NUMBER</B><BR>
* - <b>GPIO_NAME:</b> Any digital GPIO
* - <b>BUS_name:</b> A combination of multiple digital GPIOs, from 2 to 16 pins. You can combine any GPIO in the bus, but you must create it using the create_reg instruction before using this name.
* - <b>VARIABLE_NAME:</b> variable name that keeps the data
* - <b>NUMBER:</b> An integer number.
*
* <span style='color:blue'><em><B> Example:</B> </em> </span><br>
*   myvalue=0xff;<br>
*	put PA_4,  myvalue;		&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem read the value from PA_4 </span><br>
* Or:<br>
*	create_reg myreg , PA_3,PA_2,PA_10_PB3;			&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem create register</span> <br>
*	put myreg, myvalue;			&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  <span style='color:green'> rem read the Register </span> <br>
*
*
*/
